    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110031\">@Patrick Massot</span> The problem is as I guessed.  <code>Mwe</code> imports <code>Mwe.Bar</code> and <code>Mwe.Foo</code></p>\n<p><strong>Mwe.lean</strong></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mwe.Bar</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mwe.Foo</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mwe.Hello</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>Mwe.Bar</code> and <code>Mwe.Foo</code> should never be imported (as they are the roots of executables). Reemoving them fixes eveyrhting.</p>\n<p><strong>Mwe.lean</strong></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mwe</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Hello</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>With this, <code>lake build</code> now works (and <code>lake build Mwe.Hello</code>, <code>lake build Mwe.Hello:fooer</code>, and <code>lake build Hello.barer</code> continue to work). As a follow-up, updating the <code>lakefile.lean</code> as I suggested above also works without error.</p>",
        "id": 628217923,
        "sender_full_name": "Mac Malone",
        "timestamp": 1790809005
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I’m sorry it took me a long time to come back to this. Thanks Thomas and Mac for your explanations. I just realized something that was preventing me from doing the right thing: I never realized that you can have <em>multiple</em> <code>@[default_target]</code>.</p>",
        "id": 629461305,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1791274306
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The next question is: how can get profiling information when executing a facet? I’m still trying to bump an old project and I have a <em>huge</em> performance regression (at least 1000x). I have no idea how to find what is now taking forever appart from inserting explicit timing instruction everywhere in my program. Is there an analogue of <code>set_option profiler true</code> and friends in this context?</p>",
        "id": 629470548,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1791276445
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I’m still interested in the general answer to the above question, but the issue that prompted it turned out to be <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/pull/15543\">lean4#15543</a>.</p>",
        "id": 629899902,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1791389398
